rpresser <rpres...@gmail.com> wrote:

> The patch I'm thinking of would allow multiple
> bones files to be saved for each level. It would
> work thus:

> 1) When loading a level, if there is more than one
> bones file for the level, pick one at random, with
> the usual chance of not loading any.  Unlink it as
> usual after loading.  2) When the player dies, and
> the game has decided to save a bones file, if
> there is already a bones file saved for this
> level, just generate a new name.  (Append a
> letter, perhaps.)

> It doesn't seem technically too difficult to
> implement. Is it too meaningless to worry about?

No, it's not meaningless.

Right now, you can only drop a bones if there isn't
an existing one, decreasing the 1/3rd chance of
dropping bones on a bones eligible level by the
proportion of them already occupied by bones.
Without your change, then, the chance of dropping
bones is smaller.

Right now, you can only acquire a bones file when
there is one in the slot for the level, and if so,
only 1/3rd of the time.

Right now, when you pick up a bones file, the file
is consumed, and the level's bones file slot is
always empty afterwards until a new bones file is
dropped. With your proposal, sometimes it would
_not_ be empty afterwards, making it possible for
the very next player to get a bones file from that
level, so you've also increased the chances per
level of acquiring a bones file.

Since I play that way, keeping the bones file slots
for all levels for which I have bones files at all,
always full at the start of each game, I can affirm
that its a lot of fun.

I can also imagine, since some people mention always
cleaning out all bones files, that it's strictly an
acquired taste.

